        "original_id": "485fbd91-a4ee-5507-8cf7-b3957556b3bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hal McRae\n- Organizations: Kansas City Royals, Cincinnati Reds, Tampa Bay Devil Rays, Major League Baseball\n- Roles: left fielder, manager\n- Events: Kansas City Royals founding, World Series appearances, 2002 Tampa Bay Devil Rays season\n\nFacts:\n- Hal McRae was born on July 10, 1945.\n- The Kansas City Royals were founded in 1969 as an expansion franchise.\n- Hal McRae played as a left fielder in Major League Baseball for the Cincinnati Reds in 1968 and from 1970 to 1972.\n- Hal McRae played as a left fielder in Major League Baseball for the Kansas City Royals from 1973 to 1987.\n- The Kansas City Royals lost the World Series in 1980.\n- The Kansas City Royals won the World Series in 1985.\n- In the 2002 Tampa Bay Devil Rays season, Hal McRae was the manager in his first full and last season with the team.\n- The Kansas City Royals lost the World Series in 2014.\n- The Kansas City Royals won the World Series in 2015.",
